ormula for cosine with $u=x$ and $v=\\frac{4\\pi }{3}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+\\frac{4\\pi }{3}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{4\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{4\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-332521/field-1" "q-332521/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "831f9aa0-099e-5e0c-8a9d-c4828b629f64"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332521"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
